 as the state of the captives. (Theodoret) (Calmet)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","My heart, &c. Is not repeated in Hebrew. But it is, [in] Psalm lvi. 8."],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Arise, my glory. Is found also in this psalm, though not here in Hebrew, &c. St. Jerome (ad Sun.) thinks some copyist has inserted it. (Calmet) — But it seems to be here in its proper place. (Berthier)"],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Nations. David made various conquests, which prefigured those of Christ, to whom the rest of the psalm belongs. (St. Augustine) (Worthington)"],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","That. See Psalm lix. 7. (Worthington)"],["haydock",8,null,"haydock","Holiness. Or holy one, sancto: (Haydock) meaning Jeremias xxv. 11., who foretold the end of the captivity, (Calmet) or David himself, and the Messias, his son, in whom he will rejoice. (Haydock)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}